  "verbalization": "Pandaroside G appears to have a shared mechanism of action with other compounds that target the glucagon receptor, as evidenced by its interaction with Jurkat cells, which are subsequently targeted by Schisandilactone G and Oleodaphnone. These compounds all lead to the glucagon receptor, suggesting a common pathway in which the receptor is a downstream target. The evidence indicates that Pandaroside G may act through a similar mechanism, possibly by modulating signaling pathways that ultimately lead to glucagon receptor activation. The high scores in all three paths suggest a consistent relationship, though the exact mechanism remains to be fully elucidated. The integration of these findings implies that Pandaroside G could be part of a broader class of compounds that influence the glucagon receptor, potentially through a shared biological process.",
